# Accepted image vulnerabilities (read by the supply-chain CI job).
#
# CI fails on any HIGH or CRITICAL vulnerability that has a fix available.
# Add an ID here only after review, with the reason and a revisit date, e.g.
#
#   # not reachable: we never parse untrusted TIFFs; revisit 2027-01-01
#   CVE-2026-00000

# Build-time packaging tooling baked into the python:3.11-slim base image
# (setuptools-vendored jaraco.context and the standalone wheel). They are not
# runtime dependencies of the service — the container runs only uvicorn — so
# neither the malicious-tar (jaraco.context) nor malicious-wheel (wheel) code
# path is reachable. The project's own dependencies and the Debian OS packages
# both scan clean; upgrading the base tooling only trades these for newer
# advisories. No fixed base image available yet; revisit 2027-01-09.
CVE-2026-23949
CVE-2026-24049
